Fix missing <cstdint> include in the DRAMsim3 wrapper (GCC 13+ build fix).

    @tandonmitul27

WHY THIS IS NEEDED
    gem5 25.1's dramsim3_wrapper.hh uses fixed-width integer types
    (uint64_t, uint8_t) but never includes <cstdint>.  Older libstdc++
    pulled it in transitively through <string>/<functional>; GCC 13
    tightened its transitive includes, so the file no longer compiles.
    Without this patch `scons build/NULL/gem5.opt` fails with
    "'uint64_t' does not name a type" as soon as DRAMsim3 is enabled.

    Upstream-agnostic: adding a missing include is always correct, and
    the patch is a no-op on toolchains that already provided it.

diff --git a/src/mem/dramsim3_wrapper.hh b/src/mem/dramsim3_wrapper.hh
index 41b1088..81bf0c0 100644
--- a/src/mem/dramsim3_wrapper.hh
+++ b/src/mem/dramsim3_wrapper.hh
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@
 #ifndef __MEM_DRAMSIM3_WRAPPER_HH__
 #define __MEM_DRAMSIM3_WRAPPER_HH__
 
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <functional>
 #include <string>
 
